- op: discuss  # cb35
  at: '2026-03-19T05:59:47Z'  # cb35
  by: agent  # cb35
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cb35
  clock: 24  # cb35
  nonce: cb35  # cb35
  message: "Rigorous comparison complete: tested 7 repos (flask-restful, prometheus, django, killbill, ripgrep, harbor, kafka). Result: **sketches are identical with and without edge-type weighting.**\n\nRoot cause: `rank_symbols()` already has `exclude_import_edges=True` which filters out import/imports_module edges entirely. Since calls (weight 1.0) are the dominant remaining edge type, the weighting has no effect on rankings.\n\nThe weighting would matter if we changed to `exclude_import_edges=False` and used weights instead of binary filtering. This is a smoother approach (imports contribute 0.3 instead of 0.0) but the current binary filtering works well.\n\n**Assessment: the change is safe (no regressions) but currently has no observable effect.** It's a correct infrastructure addition that will become valuable when/if we switch from binary import exclusion to weighted inclusion. No user-facing impact to worry about."  # cb35
